2 0 obj
<<
/Producer (PyPDF2)
/Title (Individual\040differences\040in\040automatic\040semantic\040priming\056)
/Author (Sally\040Andrews\054\040Steson\040Lo\054\040Violet\040Xia)
/Subject (This\040research\040investigated\040whether\040masked\040semantic\040priming\040in\040a\040semantic\040categorization\040task\040that\040required\040classification\040of\040words\040as\040animals\040or\040nonanimals\040was\040modulated\040by\040individual\040differences\040in\040lexical\040proficiency\056\040A\040sample\040of\04089\040skilled\040readers\054\040assessed\040on\040reading\040comprehension\054\040vocabulary\040and\040spelling\040ability\054\040classified\040target\040words\040preceded\040by\040brief\040\05050\040ms\051\040masked\040primes\040that\040were\040either\040congruent\040or\040incongruent\040with\040the\040category\040of\040the\040target\056\040Congruent\040primes\040were\040also\040selected\040to\040be\040either\040high\040\050e\056g\056\054\040hawk\040EAGLE\054\040pistol\040RIFLE\051\040or\040low\040\050e\056g\056\054\040mole\040EAGLE\054\040boots\040RIFLE\051\040in\040semantic\040feature\040overlap\040with\040the\040target\056\040\042Overall\040proficiency\054\042\040indexed\040by\040high\040performance\040on\040both\040a\040\042semantic\040composite\042\040measure\040of\040reading\040comprehension\040and\040vocabulary\040and\040a\040\042spelling\040composite\054\042\040was\040associated\040with\040stronger\040congruence\040priming\040from\040both\040high\040and\040low\040feature\040overlap\040primes\040for\040animal\040exemplars\054\040but\040only\040predicted\040priming\040from\040low\040overlap\040primes\040for\040nonexemplars\056\040Classification\040of\040high\040frequency\040nonexemplars\040was\040also\040significantly\040modulated\040by\040an\040independent\040\042spelling\055meaning\042\040factor\054\040indexed\040by\040the\040discrepancy\040between\040the\040semantic\040and\040spelling\040composites\054\040because\040relatively\040higher\040scores\040on\040the\040semantic\040than\040the\040spelling\040composite\040were\040associated\040with\040stronger\040semantic\040priming\056\040These\040findings\040show\040that\040higher\040lexical\040proficiency\040is\040associated\040with\040stronger\040evidence\040of\040automatic\040semantic\040priming\040and\040suggest\040that\040individual\040differences\040in\040lexical\040quality\040modulate\040the\040division\040of\040labor\040between\040orthographic\040and\040semantic\040processing\040in\040early\040lexical\040retrieval\056\040\050PsycINFO\040Database\040Record)
/Keywords (06\040Mar\0402017\054\040Journal\040of\040Experimental\040Psychology\072\040Human\040Perception\040and\040Performance\054\040Semantic\040feature\054\040Priming\040\050psychology\051\054\040Semantic\040memory\054\040Spelling\054\040University\040of\040Sydney)
>>
endobj
